{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "label": "TCP", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "label": "TcpSocketActor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Dials a remote host and owns one connection; inbound frames go straight to the target with no subscribe command and no envelope \u2014 each message IS the frame.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "label": "TcpServerActor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Binds a port and serves every accepted connection, built on the same cross-runtime TCP layer the cluster transport uses so Bun, Node, Deno and TLS come from one place. With bindPort 0 the OS picks and boundPort reads it back.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcpframing", "label": "TcpFraming strategies", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "bytes, lines and length-prefixed are chosen with a config union, not framer classes. maxLineLen caps a line in BYTES including the un-terminated one, which is what bounds the re-assembly buffer against a peer that never sends a delimiter; an empty delimiter is rejected because it matches at every offset without consuming anything \u2014 a wedged process, not a slow framer. Framing is validated at start so a bad setting throws OptionsError before a socket exists. On the server it is applied per accepted connection, each with its own buffer, so two clients mid-frame never splice.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcpservermessage", "label": "TcpServerMessage union", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A listener has many connections, so every message names the one it belongs to via connectionId. connectionClosed arrives for every ending \u2014 peer hangup, error, an explicit close, a breached frame cap, or the actor stopping \u2014 so there is one signal and one code path.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_connection_id_not_actor", "label": "connectionId instead of one actor per connection", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "An actor's restart semantics do not apply to a socket \u2014 a restarted connection actor cannot resurrect the peer's TCP connection. The target is free to spawn a child per connectionOpened when it wants per-connection state; nothing forces the allocation.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_maxconnections", "label": "maxConnections admission cap", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A connection arriving at the cap is ABORTED rather than registered. An orderly close only sends a FIN and a peer that never answers keeps the socket and its file descriptor alive; since that socket was never registered the cap would not count it either, so a half-close would bound only cooperating peers. The refused peer therefore sees a connection error \u2014 what being turned away at capacity looks like at the TCP level.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_outbound_buffer_zero", "label": "Listener outboundBuffer defaults to 0", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Buffering while disconnected exists so a message survives a reconnect, but 'disconnected' for a listener means the port is down, which means every connection it accepted is already gone \u2014 so a buffered write names an id that can never come back. A BrokerNotConnected event says that; a replay would not.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tls_material", "label": "TCP server TLS material", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "tls carries certificate MATERIAL \u2014 PEM contents or DER bytes, never a path. A half-configured credential (cert with no key, or a ca alone) is rejected at start rather than quietly bound in plaintext, and there is deliberately no HOCON leaf because a config file is the wrong place for a private key.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcpframing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcpservermessage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_connection_id_not_actor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_maxconnections", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_outbound_buffer_zero", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tls_material", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_overview_io_overview", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_broker_actor_base", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_tcp_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_udp_udp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRA